---
description: How to cut a release — changesets and conventional commits for GenCore packages
---

# Release process

- Version bumps go through [Changesets](https://github.com/changesets/changesets):
  run the `cut-changeset` skill / `pnpm changeset` and describe the change from the
  consumer's point of view.
- Commit messages follow Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, etc.) —
  enforced by commitlint on `commit-msg`.
- Only `@gencore/*` **packages** are published/versioned via changesets. Apps
  (`apps/terminal`, `apps/explorer`) stay `"private": true` and are never published —
  they don't need changesets for internal-only changes, but a changeset is still
  required if an app change accompanies a package version bump.
- Do not hand-edit `CHANGELOG.md` files; they are generated by `changeset version`.
- Do not skip the changeset for a `@gencore/*` package change just because it's small —
  patch-level changesets are cheap and keep the changelog accurate.
